Chile's Senate Economy Committee backs a full ban on online gambling

The committee approved two amendments by 3 votes to 1, with 1 abstention, and plans to merge them at its next session. One version would prohibit operating, offering or advertising online betting platforms, with state lotteries, racetracks and land-based casinos exempt. The government had proposed licensing private operators with five-year licences and 19% VAT; the bill now goes line by line before the Finance Committee.

